Good.

Now add midground trees and hedgerow behind enemy line. In world.js createTreeLine, add clusters at z=-28..-40, x spread. But the enemy line at z=-17; trees at z=-30 will appear behind them, framing. Need to avoid blocking the road center. Place clusters on far left/right and a few center-back. Use lowDetail true.

Add:
```
for (let i=0;i<10;i++) {
  const side = i%2?1:-1
  createTree(scene, side*rand(12,40), -30-rand(0,12), rand(0.9,1.4), 'oak', true)
}
```
Also hedgerow as low bushes along z=-27 from x -40..-10 and 10..40, using icosahedron. Could add function createHedgerow. Simple group of low green blobs, merged? Use instanced? It's okay to add 60 meshes but draw calls. Use merged geometry with one material. Let's implement createHedgerow with merged icosahedrons.

Simpler: add a `createBushLine` using InstancedMesh of icosahedron (radius 1) with 120 instances along z=-26, scaled 1-2.5 wide, 0.7-1.5 high, colors dark green. Instanced one draw call.

Also add some near foreground bushes to frame edges? Maybe not.

Let's add in World constructor after createTreeLine:
```
createHedgerow(scene)
```
Function:
```
function createHedgerow(scene) {
  const geo = new THREE.IcosahedronGeometry(1, 0)
  const mat = new THREE.MeshStandardMaterial({ color: 0x33452a, roughness: 1, flatShading: true })
  const count = 150
  const mesh = new THREE.InstancedMesh(geo, mat, count)
  const color = new THREE.Color()
  for (let i=0;i<count;i++){
    let x,z
    if (i<75) { x = rand(-44,-10); z = -26 - rand(0,2.5) }
    else { x = rand(10,44); z = -26 - rand(0,2.5) }
    // gap around x -2..2? already outside.
    const y = terrainHeight(x,z)
    const s = rand(0.7,1.6)
    _m4.compose(_v.set(x, y + s*0.35, z), _q.setFromEuler(_e.set(0,rand(0,TAU),0)), _s.set(s*rand(1.2,2.2), s*rand(0.6,1.0), s*rand(0.9,1.6)))
    mesh.setMatrixAt(i,_m4)
    color.setHSL(0.22+rand(-0.02,0.02), rand(0.2,0.38), rand(0.16,0.28))
    mesh.setColorAt(i,color)
  }
  ...
}
```
This creates a hedge band at z=-26. But the enemy line at z=-17 will be in front. Good. However hedge at z=-26 could block advancing enemy flanks at z=-31? They'll walk through; visual only.

Actually the hedge would hide the distant crowd and treeline, adding a nice dark band at horizon. Good.

But be careful not to make it look like a green wall. Use gaps and varied heights.

Also add a few tall trees behind the hedge at z=-32..-45. The treeLine already at -72. Add 8 mid trees.

Let's implement.

